# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/hollowstar/agents.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event ga_grey_gloves
# en: Grey Gloves
title [f1b558] = 灰手套
# en: There is a pair of grey kid gloves folded on your pillow, and the fingertips are white with frost. The card beside them says, in a beautiful hand: "For cold hands. They will need to be steady." The room is warm. The gloves are not.
text [569788] = 你的枕头上叠着一副灰色小羊皮手套，指尖结着白霜。旁边的卡片上，字迹很漂亮：“给冰冷的手。它们得稳住。”房间里很暖。手套不暖。
# en: A pair of grey kid gloves folded on a dormitory pillow, a rime of frost on the fingertips, a card beside them in a beautiful hand.
scene [b124c1] = 宿舍枕头上叠着一副灰色小羊皮手套，指尖覆着一层白霜，旁边一张卡片上是漂亮的字迹。
# en: Put them on
opt.left.label [4280ed] = 戴上
# en: Hollow. Your spells, his gloves.
opt.left.hint [54f442] = 空洞。你的咒语，他的手套。
# en: They fit as if they'd been made for you, and perhaps they were. Spells come out of your fingers clean and cold and exactly where you meant. By the evening you can't feel your knuckles. In the morning the gloves are gone from the chair where you left them, and your hands are warm again, and you miss the cold.
opt.left.say.1 [675fd5] = 它们合手得像是为你量身做的，也许正是。咒语从你指间出来，干净、冰冷，正落在你想要的地方。到傍晚，你的指节已经没了知觉。第二天早上，你放在椅子上的手套不见了，手又暖了回来，而你竟想念那份冷。
# en: Drop them in the lake
opt.right.label [bb278d] = 扔进湖里
# en: Lumen. He'll know.
opt.right.hint [36edbb] = 流明。他会知道的。
# en: You throw them off the end of the jetty. They don't sink. They float, palm up, for a long time, until the light goes, and you're fairly sure they're still there in the morning.
opt.right.say.1 [bd5b27] = 你从码头尽头把它们扔了出去。它们没有沉。它们掌心朝上浮着，浮了很久，直到天色暗下去，你几乎可以肯定，第二天早上它们还在那儿。

@event ga_grey_board
# en: Paid by Family
title [19b5a4] = 家人代付
# en: The bursar's clerk calls you back to the window and slides this month's board money across to you. "It's been paid," she says. "A gentleman in grey. He said he was family." The receipt isn't signed. Where the name should be there's a single thumbprint, white with frost.
text [ccc0d0] = 财务处的办事员把你叫回窗口，把这个月的膳宿费推回给你。“已经有人付了，”她说，“一位穿灰衣的先生。他说他是家人。”收据上没有签名。该签名的地方只有一个指印，白得像霜。
# en: A bursar's window, a clerk holding out a small stack of coins and a receipt, a student staring at a signature in a beautiful hand.
scene [f7691f] = 财务处的窗口，一个办事员递出一小摞硬币和一张收据，一个学生盯着上面漂亮的字迹。
# en: Keep the money
opt.left.label [b1f08b] = 把钱收下
# en: Hollow. Family looks after its own.
opt.left.hint [13f3fa] = 空洞。家人照顾自己人。
# en: You put the coins in your purse. They're cold, and they stay cold all month, and you find you spend them last.
opt.left.say.1 [45c3fc] = 你把硬币放进钱袋。它们是冷的，一整个月都冷，你发现自己总是最后才花它们。
# en: Have it sent back to him
opt.right.label [236eb4] = 让他们退给他
# en: Lumen. You pay your own way.
opt.right.hint [b5b4ab] = 流明。你自己的路自己付。
# en: "Sent back where?" says the clerk. You don't know. In the end she puts the coins in an envelope marked RETURN TO SENDER and pins it to the board behind her. In the morning the envelope is gone, and the pin is white with frost.
opt.right.say.1 [ff914f] = “退到哪儿去？”办事员问。你不知道。最后她把硬币装进一个写着“退回寄件人”的信封，钉在身后的布告板上。第二天早上信封不见了，那枚图钉白得像霜。

@event ga_grey_witness
# en: Children Talk
title [3b6060] = 孩子们会说话
# en: The courtyard fountain freezes as you pass, and the man in grey is sitting on its rim. "A first-year has been telling people she saw us talking," he says pleasantly. "Children talk. It worries the families. What would you do about it, if it were yours to do?"
text [e8bb63] = 你经过时，庭院的喷泉冻住了，灰衣人坐在池沿上。“有个一年级女生在跟人说，她看见我们在说话，”他客客气气地说，“孩子们会说话。这让世家担心。要是由你来处理，你会怎么做？”
# en: A frozen courtyard fountain at dusk, a tall man in a grey coat on its rim, a student standing in front of him, a first-year hurrying away across the flagstones behind them.
scene [8182d6] = 黄昏时冻住的庭院喷泉，一个穿灰外套的高个男人坐在池沿上，一个学生站在他面前，一个一年级生在他们身后匆匆穿过石板地。
# en: "Leave her alone."
opt.left.label [0720bc] = “别管她。”
# en: Lumen. He'll take it as an answer.
opt.left.hint [7ea37b] = 流明。他会把这当作答复。
# en: "Of course," he says, as if you'd passed or failed something, and you can't tell which. He gets up and walks away through the gate. The fountain doesn't thaw until morning.
opt.left.say.1 [aa9f76] = “当然，”他说，好像你通过了或没通过什么，你分辨不出是哪个。他起身，从大门走了出去。喷泉直到早上才化冻。
# en: "I'll make sure she stops."
opt.right.label [437329] = “我会让她闭嘴。”
# en: Hollow. It works.
opt.right.hint [36aea7] = 空洞。管用。
# en: You find her after supper and tell her, quietly, what happens to people who talk about things they don't understand. You don't know where the words come from. She doesn't talk again. She doesn't look at you again, either.
opt.right.say.1 [7bfce3] = 晚饭后你找到她，轻声告诉她，谈论自己不懂的事的人会有什么下场。你不知道这些话从哪儿来的。她再也没说过。她也再没看过你一眼。

@event ga_grey_question
# en: At the End of the Table
title [de4d84] = 长凳的另一头
# en: At supper the water in the jugs along your table has frozen solid, and nobody seems to notice. Nor do they notice the man in grey at the far end of the bench, his gloved hands folded. "One question," he says, quite quietly, and his voice carries to you and no one else. "What do you want, more than anything? The truth, please. I'll know."
text [ea5826] = 晚饭时，你们这张桌上的水壶里，水全冻成了冰，可谁都没注意到。他们也没注意到长凳另一头的灰衣人，戴着手套的双手交叠着。“一个问题，”他说，声音很轻，却只传到你一个人耳朵里，“你最想要的是什么？请说实话。我会知道的。”
# en: A long refectory table at supper, students talking and passing dishes, a tall man in a grey coat sitting at its far end whom nobody else seems to see, the water in every jug iced over.
scene [132e67] = 晚饭时的膳堂长桌，学生们说着话、传着菜，一个穿灰外套的高个男人坐在桌子另一头，似乎只有一个人看得见他，每只水壶里的水都结了冰。
# en: Tell him the truth
opt.left.label [48bf7e] = 告诉他实话
# en: Hollow. He'll remember it.
opt.left.hint [c377f2] = 空洞。他会记住的。
# en: You tell him. It's easier than it should be, and you hear yourself say things you've never said aloud. He listens without interrupting, and nods once, as if writing it down. When you look up from your plate the end of the bench is empty, and the jugs are pouring water again.
opt.left.say.1 [b8174c] = 你告诉了他。比应有的容易，你听见自己说出了从没大声说过的话。他一直听着，没有打断，最后点了一下头，像是记了下来。等你从盘子上抬起头，长凳那头已经空了，水壶又倒得出水了。
# en: Lie to him
opt.right.label [c2bfa8] = 对他撒谎
# en: Lumen, a little. He may know.
opt.right.hint [70c1c4] = 流明，一点点。他也许知道。
# en: You give him something plausible, and keep your face still. He smiles, very slightly. "Good," he says. "People who lie to me last longer." Then the student next to you asks you to pass the salt, and when you turn back there's no one there.
opt.right.say.1 [3b2e9e] = 你给了他一个说得过去的答案，脸上不动声色。他微微一笑。“很好，”他说，“对我撒谎的人活得更久。”这时身边的同学请你递一下盐，等你转回头，那儿已经没人了。

@event ga_grey_ice_seat
# en: A Seat Kept Cold
title [d474c7] = 一张冷着的座椅
# en: This morning the courtyard fountain has frozen into the shape of a chair: high-backed, carved, glittering, facing the lake. Students give it a wide berth. There's no note, and there doesn't need to be.
text [ae0db2] = 今天早上，庭院的喷泉冻成了一把椅子的形状：高靠背，带雕花，晶莹发亮，面朝湖水。学生们都绕着它走。没有留言，也不需要。
# en: A courtyard fountain frozen into the shape of a high-backed chair, glittering in the morning, students walking a wide circle round it.
scene [6a7d00] = 庭院喷泉冻成了一把高背椅的形状，在晨光中闪闪发亮，学生们绕着它远远走开。
# en: Sit in it
opt.left.label [3fceaf] = 坐上去
# en: Hollow. It doesn't feel cold.
opt.left.hint [0ee71d] = 空洞。它不觉得冷。
# en: You sit down in front of half the courtyard. It isn't cold at all. It's like sitting in the sun. From the chair the lake looks very close, and very calm, and you stay longer than you mean to, while people stare.
opt.left.say.1 [f1f823] = 你当着半个庭院的人坐了下去。一点也不冷。像坐在阳光里。从椅子上看，湖显得很近，很平静，你坐得比打算的久，任人盯着看。
# en: Break it with your heel
opt.right.label [1516c4] = 用鞋跟把它踢碎
# en: Lumen. It hurts.
opt.right.hint [797817] = 流明。会疼。
# en: It takes six kicks, and the last one hurts all the way up to your knee. The ice breaks into a thousand pieces that don't melt for a day. A first-year sweeps them up, and asks you, nervously, whether it was yours.
opt.right.say.1 [af2d84] = 踢了六下，最后一下疼得一直传到膝盖。冰碎成了上千块，过了一整天都没化。一个一年级生把碎冰扫起来，怯生生地问你，那是不是你的。

@event wa_tower_light
# en: A Light in the Tower
title [5a4f19] = 塔里的灯
# en: Crossing the courtyard late, you look up: there's one lit window at the top of the headmistress's tower, and someone standing at it, watching you all the way across. In the morning there's a card under your door, in a neat, unhurried hand: "Bed by midnight. The castle is not always kind after it. — I.M."
text [ca98e9] = 深夜穿过庭院时，你抬头一看：院长塔顶亮着一扇窗，有人站在窗前，一直看着你走过整个庭院。第二天早上，你门缝底下塞着一张卡片，字迹工整从容：“午夜前上床。过了午夜，城堡并不总是友善。——伊·马”
# en: A dark courtyard at night, a student crossing it, one lit window high in a tower above with a tall figure standing at the glass.
scene [f4992a] = 夜里漆黑的庭院，一个学生正穿过，高处塔上亮着一扇窗，一个高挑的身影站在玻璃后面。
# en: Keep to it
opt.left.label [8e27de] = 照做
# en: You're in bed by midnight for a month, which surprises everyone, you most. Once, coming back with a minute to spare, you look up and the window goes dark, as if someone had been waiting to see.
opt.left.say.1 [f2ae1b] = 一整个月你都在午夜前上床，所有人都很意外，你自己最意外。有一次，你只差一分钟赶回来，抬头时那扇窗正好暗了，像是有人一直在等着看。
# en: Wave at the window next time
opt.right.label [9b18bc] = 下次朝那扇窗挥手
# en: The next late night you stop in the middle of the courtyard and wave. After a moment, high up, a hand lifts in answer. Nobody mentions it, and you don't sleep any earlier.
opt.right.say.1 [9e24f1] = 又一个晚归的夜里，你停在庭院中央挥了挥手。过了一会儿，高处有一只手抬起来回应。谁也没提起这事，你也没有睡得更早。

@event wa_lake_word
# en: Walk Elsewhere
title [1b55e4] = 换条路走
# en: Headmistress Marrow meets you on the lakeshore path, alone, which she never is. "Walk elsewhere after dark this month," she says pleasantly. "The lake is cold this time of year." She waits, as if it were a move in a game, to see what you'll do with it.
text [e414c5] = 马罗院长在湖岸小路上迎面碰见你，独自一人，她从不独自一人。“这个月天黑以后，换条路走，”她客客气气地说，“这个时节湖水很冷。”她等着，像是下了一步棋，看你怎么应。
# en: A tall woman in dark robes stopping a student on the lakeshore path, one ringed hand raised, the lake behind them grey and very still.
scene [a7335e] = 一个穿深色长袍的高挑女人在湖岸小路上拦住一个学生，一只戴着戒指的手微微抬起，身后的湖灰蒙蒙的，静得出奇。
# en: Promise her
opt.left.label [5111dd] = 答应她
# en: "Thank you," she says, and seems to mean more than the words. You keep away from the water all month. Some nights you hear the lake through your window, and it sounds like something turning over in its sleep.
opt.left.say.1 [070cd9] = “谢谢你，”她说，似乎意思比话更多。一整个月你都远离水边。有些夜里，你隔着窗听见湖声，像是有什么东西在睡梦里翻了个身。
# en: "Why this month?"
opt.right.label [e92b68] = “为什么是这个月？”
# en: Her short, delighted laugh. "Because I asked you," she says, "and because you asked me why. Both good signs." She tells you nothing else. You walk the long way round for a month anyway.
opt.right.say.1 [34fe57] = 她那短促而开心的笑。“因为我请你这么做，”她说，“也因为你问了我为什么。两样都是好兆头。”她别的什么也没说。你还是绕了一个月的远路。

@event wa_isolde_list
# en: The List
title [068fdc] = 名单
# en: Headmistress Marrow has sent for you, and keeps you waiting while she writes. On the desk, upside down, is a short list in her hand. You can read your own name on it. You can also read that the name above yours has been crossed through, recently, with a single neat line.
text [645692] = 马罗院长叫你过去，又让你等着，自己在写东西。桌上倒放着一张她亲笔写的短名单。你能认出上面有你的名字。你也能认出，你上面的那个名字最近被划掉了，一道干净利落的线。
# en: A headmistress's study at dusk, a short handwritten list on the desk, one name near the bottom crossed through with a single neat line.
scene [e10e79] = 黄昏时院长的书房，桌上一张手写的短名单，靠下的一个名字被一道干净利落的线划掉了。
# en: Ask whose name it was
opt.left.label [363297] = 问那是谁的名字
# en: She doesn't look up. "Someone who changed their mind," she says. "People do. It's allowed. Lists are not promises." Then she sets you an essay on the history of the castle's wards and sends you away, and the list goes into a drawer.
opt.left.say.1 [3c7881] = 她没抬头。“一个改了主意的人，”她说，“人会改主意。这是允许的。名单不是承诺。”然后她给你布置了一篇关于城堡护界历史的论文，打发你走了，名单收进了抽屉。
# en: Say nothing, and wait
opt.right.label [757d4b] = 什么也不说，等着
# en: You wait. She finishes, blots, and folds the list away without a word. Then she asks after your marks, and your sleep, and your friends, by name, as if checking each off. "Good," she says. "Keep it that way."
opt.right.say.1 [5d7dfb] = 你等着。她写完，吸干墨迹，一言不发地把名单折起收好。然后她问起你的成绩、你的睡眠、你的朋友，一个个点名问，像在逐一核对。“很好，”她说，“保持下去。”

@event wa_thorne_note
# en: By Hand, Not by Owl
title [8a4cc9] = 亲手送，别用猫头鹰
# en: Professor Thorne stops you on the library stair after supper and holds out a small folded note, sealed with plain wax. "Old Maud," he says. "Tonight. By hand, not by owl." He doesn't explain. The silver ring on his hand catches the lamp. "Hm. And don't read it."
text [1b05c1] = 晚饭后，索恩教授在图书馆楼梯上拦住你，递出一张折好的小字条，用普通的蜡封着。“老莫德，”他说，“今晚。亲手送，别用猫头鹰。”他没解释。他手上的银戒指在灯下一闪。“嗯。别看。”
# en: A library stair in the evening, a stern professor with a silver ring holding out a small sealed note to a student, the window behind him dark over the lake.
scene [c42a6b] = 傍晚的图书馆楼梯，一位戴银戒指的严肃教授把一张封好的小字条递给一个学生，他身后的窗外是漆黑的湖面。
# en: Take it down to her now
opt.left.label [874151] = 现在就送下去
# en: It's a cold walk to the cottage in the dark. Maud reads the note on her doorstep by the light of her door, folds it once and puts it in the stove. Then she gives you a cup of something hot and sends you back up the hill. Next morning Thorne says nothing, which from Thorne is thanks.
opt.left.say.1 [73f145] = 在黑暗里走到小屋，一路很冷。莫德就着门口的光在台阶上读完字条，折了一下，塞进炉子里。然后她给你倒了杯热乎乎的东西，打发你回山上去。第二天早上索恩什么也没说，这在索恩就算道谢了。
# en: Take it at first light instead
opt.right.label [7d5118] = 改到天亮再送
# en: The lake path in the dark is no place to be, you tell yourself, and you sleep, and go at first light. Maud opens the door at dawn already dressed, reads the note on her step, and burns it in the stove. "He said tonight, dearie," she says. Thorne, at breakfast, doesn't look at you at all.
opt.right.say.1 [7c8a41] = 你告诉自己，黑夜里的湖边小路不是该走的地方，于是先睡了，天一亮才去。莫德开门时已经穿戴整齐，在台阶上读了字条，把它烧进了炉子。“他说的是今晚，孩子，”她说。早饭时，索恩看都没看你一眼。

@event wa_maud_lantern
# en: For Walking Near Water
title [309160] = 走近水边时用
# en: Old Maud is waiting at her gate as you pass, with a small brass lantern in her hand and a silver ring on the hand holding it. "There you are, dearie," she says. "Take this. For walking near water. It's old. It's seen worse nights than this one."
text [774c8a] = 你路过时，老莫德正等在她的院门口，手里提着一盏小铜灯，提灯的那只手上戴着一枚银戒指。“你来了，孩子，”她说，“拿着。走近水边的时候用。它老了。比今晚更糟的夜它都见过。”
# en: A cottage doorway at dusk, an old woman with a silver ring on an earthy hand holding out a small brass lantern to a student.
scene [075c69] = 黄昏时小屋的门口，一位手上沾着泥土、戴着银戒指的老妇人把一盏小铜灯递给一个学生。
# en: Take it and walk her in
opt.left.label [271b5f] = 接过来，送她进屋
# en: You walk her up her own path and she talks all the way about her beans, except once, at the bend where you can see the lake, where she stops talking altogether. You give her the lantern back at her door; she only wanted it carried. You think about that bend a fortnight later, on the lakeshore at dusk.
opt.left.say.1 [f70e52] = 你陪她走上她自家的小路，她一路都在讲她的豆子，只有一次，在能望见湖的那个拐弯处，她完全不说话了。到了门口你把灯还给她；她只是想有人帮她提着。两个星期后，黄昏时你走在湖岸上，想起了那个拐弯。
# en: Thank her, and go
opt.right.label [03f98d] = 谢过她，走了
# en: "Mind it doesn't go out," she says, and shuts the gate. The lantern burns all night on your sill without being filled. In the morning it's cold, and when you take it back to her gate she takes it as if she'd expected to.
opt.right.say.1 [b79750] = “当心别让它灭了，”她说，关上了院门。那盏灯在你的窗台上没添油却亮了一整夜。到早上它凉了，你把它送回她门口，她接过去，好像早料到你会来。
